test_tcp_park — TCP send-buf parking self-test
================================================

Phase 1 of the net-stack quality plan added real parking to
`inet_handle_tcp_send`: when the send buffer is full, the inet
server parks the caller in `send_waiter` instead of replying
with `n=0`, and the ACK-handling path wakes the parked caller
once any space frees up.

This test triggers the inet self-test that drives the park/wake
state machine synthetically — no real TCP connection needed.
The self-test runs entirely inside the inet server: it forces a
scratch slot ESTABLISHED with a full send_buf, parks a fake
waiter, drains the buffer, and verifies the ACK-path drain
helper clears the parked slot.

Prints `tcp_park: ok` on pass or `tcp_park: failed N` where N is
the failure-step code returned by the inet self-test.

    module oskit.bin.test_tcp_park

    import oskit.ulib.{puts, exit, exit_with}
    import oskit.net.{tcp_send_park_test}


    print_udec(v: int)
        if v >= 10
            print_udec(v / 10)
        var b: [1]byte
        b[0] = byte('0' + (v % 10))
        puts(string(&b[0], 1))


    fail(code: int)
        puts("tcp_park: failed ")
        print_udec(code)
        puts("\n")
        exit_with(code)


    main(argv: []string)
        val rc = tcp_send_park_test()
        if rc != 0
            fail(rc)
            return
        puts("tcp_park: ok\n")
        exit()
